yne Campus Facilities Catering & Food Services Lodging Options Conferences & Meetings Retreats & Camps Weddings & Banquets News & Media News Brand Toolkit Media Relations Bring the whole family Homecoming Info for: Future Spartans Current Students Parents & Counselors Faculty & Staff Alumni Home > Faculty & Staff Give Request Info Visit Apply Faculty & Staff In This Section Grants & Sponsored Programs Funding Opportunities Policies, Procedures, & Forms Tools & Resources Endowed Faculty Positions Faculty Student Summer Research Faculty Tenure & Promotion Pharmacy Program Faculty Awards CETL Class Presentations, Workshops & Assignments Recommendations & Referrals On-Campus Internship Process Checklist for New Employees Emerita Faculty Faculty & Staff Your central resource for academic, professional, and research support at Manchester University. Faculty & Staff Directory academic excellence Empowering excellence in teaching, learning, and faculty development. Academic Affairs oversees curriculum innovation, faculty evaluation and support, accreditation processes, and student academic success. We work collaboratively with departments to uphold academic standards and foster a vibrant intellectual community that supports your scholarly goals. Endowed Faculty Positions Faculty Tenure & Promotion Grants & Sponsored Programs Advance your research and institutional impact through comprehensive grant support. Whether you’re exploring funding opportunities, developing proposals, or navigating post-award compliance, our office is here to partner with you every step of the way. We provide expert guidance on grant writing, budget preparation, and regulatory requirements to turn your ideas into funded projects. Grants & Sponsored Programs Policies, Procedures & Forms Tools & Resources The Faculty-Student Summer Research grant provides support for collaborative research over a period of 10 weeks during the summer. Faculty-Student Summer Research Grants The Faculty Research and Creative Endeavor grant provides funding for projects to be completed during the summer in an area of a faculty member’s academic interest. Faculty Research & Creative Endeavor Grants IT Support At the heart of Manchester University’s digital operations, Information Technology Services (ITS) is dedicated to delivering support to keep our campuses connected and secure. Whether you’re navigating systems like Canvas, ChetAdvisor, ChetNet, or Office 365, utilizing seamless printing across campus, or seeking assistance via the Help Desk, ITS is here to assist students, faculty and staff with essential tools and user-friendly guidance. Located at both North Manchester and Fort Wayne campuses, ITS is your go‑to partner for all things tech at Manchester University. IT Support Follow Follow Follow Follow Follow Follow NORTH MANCHESTER 604 E College Ave. PO Box 365 North Manchester, IN 46962 260-982-5000 FORT WAYNE 10627 Diebold Rd. Fort Wayne, IN 46845 260-470-2700 Request Info Visit Give Apply Refer a student Jobs at Manchester University Book an Event Canvas News Bookstore Events Library Quick Links Recruit Me FERPA Title IX Privacy Policy Nondiscriminatory Policy Annual Security Reports Hazing Policy/Hazing Transparency Report ©2026 Manchester University"
