ies Catering & Food Services Lodging Options Conferences & Meetings Retreats & Camps Weddings & Banquets News & Media News & Media News Brand Toolkit Media Relations Info For: Info For: Current Students Parents & Counselors Faculty & Staff Alumni Home > Student Life > Spiritual Life > Fellowship & Ministry Groups Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid » Undergraduate Admissions First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Veterans Early College Experience Admitted Students Commit Graduate Admissions International Student Admissions Articulations & Course Equivalencies Manchester University Tuition and Fees Student Financial Services Financial Aid Scholarships & Grants Loans Federal Aid Work Study Graduate Financial Aid Award Notification Glossary FAFSA Verification Life After Manchester Apply Visit Our Campus Campus Map Food & Lodging Request More Info Experience Manchester for Yourself Schedule Your Visit Academics Academics » Programs & Degrees Online Degrees Undergraduate Studies Core Curriculum Honors Program Experiential Learning Degree in 3 Fast Track Academic Enrichment Honors & Awards Graduate Studies Plus Programs Colleges On-Demand Training Manchester University Fort Wayne Faculty & Staff Directory Student Success Academic Support Academic Calendar Graduation Career & Professional Development Registrar What programs does Manchester offer? Find your program Student Life Student Life » Housing & Dining East Hall East Street Apartments Garver Hall Helman Hall Oakwood Hall New Student Information Consolidation Spiritual Life Fellowship & Ministry Groups Spartan Stories Events Life at Manchester Campus Life Clubs & Activities Athletics & Recreation Campus Safety Manchester Together NxtGen Program on Campus Campus Support Health & Well-being Esports Join us Mondays at 11 a.m. VIA Schedule Athletics About About » MU at a Glance Mission & Values Our History Leadership Assessment & Accreditation Institutional Effectiveness Accreditation Assessment Faculty & Staff Directory Conference Services North Manchester Campus Facilities Fort Wayne Campus Facilities Catering & Food Services Lodging Options Conferences & Meetings Retreats & Camps Weddings & Banquets News & Media News Brand Toolkit Media Relations Bring the whole family Homecoming a M Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid » Undergraduate Admissions First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Veterans Early College Experience Admitted Students Commit Graduate Admissions International Student Admissions Articulations & Course Equivalencies Manchester University Tuition and Fees Student Financial Services Financial Aid Scholarships & Grants Loans Federal Aid Work Study Graduate Financial Aid Award Notification Glossary FAFSA Verification Life After Manchester Apply Visit Our Campus Campus Map Food & Lodging Request More Info Experience Manchester for Yourself Schedule Your Visit Academics Academics » Programs & Degrees Online Degrees Undergraduate Studies Core Curriculum Honors Program Experiential Learning Degree in 3 Fast Track Academic Enrichment Honors & Awards Graduate Studies Plus Programs Colleges On-Demand Training Manchester University Fort Wayne Faculty & Staff Directory Student Success Academic Support Academic Calendar Graduation Career & Professional Development Registrar What programs does Manchester offer? Find your program Student Life Student Life » Housing & Dining East Hall East Street Apartments Garver Hall Helman Hall Oakwood Hall New Student Information Consolidation Spiritual Life Fellowship & Ministry Groups Spartan Stories Events Life at Manchester Campus Life Clubs & Activities Athletics & Recreation Campus Safety Manchester Together NxtGen Program on Campus Campus Support Health & Well-being Esports Join us Mondays at 11 a.m. VIA Schedule Athletics About About » MU at a Glance Mission & Values Our History Leadership Assessment & Accreditation Institutional Effectiveness Accreditation Assessment Faculty & Staff Directory Conference Services North Manchester Campus Facilities Fort Wayne Campus Facilities Catering & Food Services Lodging Options Conferences & Meetings Retreats & Camps Weddings & Banquets News & Media News Brand Toolkit Media Relations Bring the whole family Homecoming Info for: Future Spartans Current Students Parents & Counselors Faculty & Staff Alumni Home > Student Life > Spiritual Life > Fellowship & Ministry Groups Give Request Info Visit Apply Fellowship & Ministry Groups In This Section Housing & Dining Spiritual Life Fellowship & Ministry Groups Spartan Stories Events Life at Manchester Campus Life Fellowship and Ministry Groups Manchester University has a number of ways to engage and grow in faith. Manchester Catholics Simply Brethren ROBOT Handbell Choir Other Opportunities This is an organization for all interested Catholic and non-Catholic students, faculty, and staff. The group meets periodically to provide religious education, pastoral care, mutual support, fellowship, and service to others. There is discussion, sharing, and snacks, and there are occasional retreats and special events. For more information contact: religiouslife@manchester.edu . Simply Brethren is a group dedicated to providing support and connection for Church of the Brethren students and other interested students, faculty, and staff. Simply Brethren meetings center around fellowship and include times of worship, playing games, educational events, exploring Church of the Brethren heritage, sharing, singing, discussions around current issues, and enjoying each other’s company. People of all faith traditions are invited to participate. For more information contact: religiouslife@manchester.edu . (Radically Obedient Brethren Outreach Team) This student worship team travels to area Church of the Brethren congregations, primarily during spring semester, to lead worship and visit with church members. Students preach and assist with all facets of the service while developing their ministry gifts. The goal of the Handbell Choir is to provide members the opportunity to learn, practice and perform together as a musical ensemble. Through performances both on and off campus, the Handbell Choir represents Manchester University in a positive manner to the community. The Handbell Choir is open to all students, faculty and staff regardless of musical skill or familiarity with the handbell instruments. Primary requirement for membership is attendance at weekly rehearsals and performances. Membership is limited to the number of positions available for the number of handbells used by the choir. If interested in being a part of the handbell choir contact religiouslife@manchester.edu . Short-term or longer-term book study groups, Bible studies, discussion groups, service opportunities, prayer times, groups for athletes, events with local congregations, and other places to connect faith and education are also offered periodically. See the campus ministry office to inquire about starting a group or for information. Current groups meeting regularly include: St. John’s Lutheran Church Bible Study Women’s Bible study, Sundays Men’s Bible study On Sunday mornings, students are encouraged to attend a local congregation . Group visits to a church are sometimes scheduled. For those in the Fort Wayne area, a representative sample of worship communities is available. Follow Follow Follow Follow Follow Follow NORTH MANCHESTER 604 E College Ave. PO Box 365 North Manchester, IN 46962 260-982-5000 FORT WAYNE 10627 Diebold Rd. Fort Wayne, IN 46845 260-470-2700 Request Info Visit Give Apply Refer a student Jobs at Manchester University Book an Event Canvas News Bookstore Events Library Quick Links Recruit Me FERPA Title IX Privacy Policy Nondiscriminatory Policy Annual Security Reports Hazing Policy/Hazing Transparency Report ©2026 Manchester University"
    },
